{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39836532",
      "title": "Validating User Input & Showing an Error Modal via useImperativeHandle",
      "sourceHash": "863b924416538af008d346a3f4681edf3de72af620c969b9abee7a9da6dacae6",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.944,
          "end": 2.76,
          "en": "[Maximilian Schwarzmüller] So let's now add validation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.76,
          "end": 6.27,
          "en": "for those inputs and make sure that we show an error modal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.27,
          "end": 10.023,
          "en": "if we click save with invalid values being entered here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.19,
          "end": 12.66,
          "en": "For that, we of course need to go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.66,
          "end": 16.48,
          "en": "to the new project component where we have those inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.45,
          "end": 21.96,
          "en": "and where we are extracting those values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.96,
          "end": 26.25,
          "en": "and the first step here is to validate those values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.25,
          "end": 28.35,
          "en": "Now here, I'll keep it fairly simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.35,
          "end": 32.49,
          "en": "I'll just check if entered title once we trim it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.49,
          "end": 36.24,
          "en": "to remove excess white space at the beginning and end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.24,
          "end": 37.99,
          "en": "if that's equal to an empty string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.91,
          "end": 40.62,
          "en": "which would mean that it's invalid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.62,
          "end": 42.543,
          "en": "because it's an empty value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.59,
          "end": 47.13,
          "en": "So I wanna show the modal if this condition here is met.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.13,
          "end": 48.6,
          "en": "But that's not the only case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.6,
          "end": 51.33,
          "en": "where this error modal should be shown",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.33,
          "end": 54.54,
          "en": "because it should be shown if the title is empty,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.54,
          "end": 57.6,
          "en": "or if the description's empty.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.6,
          "end": 60.873,
          "en": "So I do the same thing here, checking for emptiness.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.58,
          "end": 66.75,
          "en": "Or, of course if the entered date is empty,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.75,
          "end": 67.743,
          "en": "once we trim it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.9,
          "end": 72.513,
          "en": "If that's empty, we also wanna show that modal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.1,
          "end": 79.1,
          "en": "So in all three cases, I wanna show the error modal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 81.3,
          "end": 84.39,
          "en": "Now for that, of course, we first of all need a modal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 84.39,
          "end": 86.43,
          "en": "and therefore I'll add a new component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 86.43,
          "end": 88.773,
          "en": "which I'll name Modal.jsx.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 89.64,
          "end": 93.81,
          "en": "I'll not name it Error Modal because, at least in theory,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 93.81,
          "end": 96.24000000000001,
          "en": "that should be a reusable modal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 96.24000000000001,
          "end": 98.438,
          "en": "that could be used to show",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 98.438,
          "end": 100.65299999999999,
          "en": "other kinds of information as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 101.64,
          "end": 104.52000000000001,
          "en": "Now therefore, here in this Modal.jsx file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 104.52000000000001,
          "end": 107.973,
          "en": "I'll export a modal function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 109.65,
          "end": 114.513,
          "en": "and in there I wanna return this built-in dialogue element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 116.03999999999999,
          "end": 119.52000000000001,
          "en": "But now here I really wanna make this modal component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 119.52000000000001,
          "end": 123.6,
          "en": "as flexible as possible and therefore I'll extract",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 123.6,
          "end": 127.35,
          "en": "the children prop, which is passed to every component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 127.35,
          "end": 131.52,
          "en": "so that I can use my modal in the end as a wrapper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 131.52,
          "end": 133.44,
          "en": "around any content I want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 133.44,
          "end": 135.75,
          "en": "and that content will then be wrapped",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 135.75,
          "end": 138.153,
          "en": "by that built-in dialogue component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 139.62,
          "end": 141.32999999999998,
          "en": "But that's not all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 141.32999999999998,
          "end": 144.69,
          "en": "In addition, I wanna use the portal feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 144.69,
          "end": 148.2,
          "en": "provided by React to render this dialogue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 148.2,
          "end": 152.1,
          "en": "and the content that will be wrapped by that dialogue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 152.1,
          "end": 154.143,
          "en": "in a different place of the DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 155.73,
          "end": 157.86,
          "en": "For that, in this starting project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 157.86,
          "end": 159.84,
          "en": "in the index HTML file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 159.84,
          "end": 162.453,
          "en": "we have this modal-root div here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 165,
          "end": 169.77,
          "en": "Therefore I'll render this with that portal feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 169.77,
          "end": 174.77,
          "en": "by importing createPortal from React-dom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 177.03,
          "end": 181.68,
          "en": "And then as you learn, you simply have to wrap this JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 181.68,
          "end": 185.43,
          "en": "with createPortal like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 185.43,
          "end": 190.43,
          "en": "And as a second value, you should pass that HTML element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 190.92,
          "end": 193.533,
          "en": "where this content should be rendered in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 194.91,
          "end": 198.64,
          "en": "For that, we use a browser API, document.getElementByID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 201.24,
          "end": 205.713,
          "en": "to select this div, which has an idea of modal-root.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 207.06,
          "end": 209.073,
          "en": "So that's what I'll use here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 210.75,
          "end": 214.413,
          "en": "And with that, I have a really flexible modal here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 215.4,
          "end": 219.6,
          "en": "but now it should become even more flexible and reusable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 219.6,
          "end": 223.05,
          "en": "I wanna make sure that we can open this dialogue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 223.05,
          "end": 226.26,
          "en": "by calling a function that should be exposed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 226.26,
          "end": 227.88,
          "en": "by my custom component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 227.88,
          "end": 231.39,
          "en": "that does not require the calling component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 231.39,
          "end": 234.42000000000002,
          "en": "so another component that uses the modal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 234.42000000000002,
          "end": 237.633,
          "en": "to know that a dialogue is used internally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 238.95,
          "end": 242.04,
          "en": "That should not be information that's needed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 242.04,
          "end": 245.793,
          "en": "by the component that uses my modal component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 246.72,
          "end": 249.99,
          "en": "And you'll learn how you can build reusable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 249.99,
          "end": 252.75,
          "en": "flexible components like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 252.75,
          "end": 256.923,
          "en": "in the end by using two features provided by React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 258.39,
          "end": 261.12,
          "en": "the forwardRef feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 261.12,
          "end": 264.693,
          "en": "and the useImperativeHandle hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 266.13,
          "end": 270.06,
          "en": "Though, of course, the forwardRef function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 270.06,
          "end": 275.06,
          "en": "is only required if you're using React version 18 or older.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 276.09000000000003,
          "end": 278.25,
          "en": "If you're working in a project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 278.25,
          "end": 281.64,
          "en": "that uses at least React version 19,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 281.64,
          "end": 283.59000000000003,
          "en": "you don't need forwardRef.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 283.59000000000003,
          "end": 285.45,
          "en": "You can simply accept refs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 285.45,
          "end": 289.11,
          "en": "as regular props in your components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 289.11,
          "end": 290.82,
          "en": "ForwardRef is not needed then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 290.82,
          "end": 293.49,
          "en": "But here I'll, again, show you the code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 293.49,
          "end": 295.77,
          "en": "that will work with React 19,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 295.77,
          "end": 299.58,
          "en": "but that would also work with older React versions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 299.58,
          "end": 302.553,
          "en": "and I will use forwardRef therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 304.05,
          "end": 307.11,
          "en": "So we must wrap our component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 307.11,
          "end": 309.813,
          "en": "with forwardRef like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 311.31,
          "end": 313.95,
          "en": "And we now must store it in a separate constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 313.95,
          "end": 317.283,
          "en": "or variable, which is then exported here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 319.38,
          "end": 320.91,
          "en": "Now with that, you learned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 320.91,
          "end": 323.82,
          "en": "that this modal component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 323.82,
          "end": 326.07,
          "en": "will receive an extra parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 326.07,
          "end": 328.41,
          "en": "which will be the ref that might be set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 328.41,
          "end": 330.513,
          "en": "from outside on that component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 332.4,
          "end": 334.38,
          "en": "Now that's the first step.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 334.38,
          "end": 337.83,
          "en": "To now expose a function that can be called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 337.83,
          "end": 339.96,
          "en": "from outside this component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 339.96,
          "end": 343.19,
          "en": "we must use useImperativeHandle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 344.45,
          "end": 347.90999999999997,
          "en": "To this hook, you first pass this ref",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 347.90999999999997,
          "end": 352.90999999999997,
          "en": "which you are receiving, so this ref here is passed here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 353.61,
          "end": 355.503,
          "en": "to use imperativeHandle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 357.21,
          "end": 360.72,
          "en": "And then as a second value, you must provide a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 360.72,
          "end": 363.48,
          "en": "that will be called by React in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 363.48,
          "end": 368.34,
          "en": "where you return an object that then exposes any properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 368.34,
          "end": 373.34,
          "en": "or functions you want to expose to our components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 373.35,
          "end": 375.573,
          "en": "For example, open method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 377.76,
          "end": 380.76,
          "en": "And in this open method, we now wanna reach out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 380.76,
          "end": 384.48,
          "en": "to that dialogue and call the show modal method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 384.48,
          "end": 388.173,
          "en": "that is provided by that built-in dialogue component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 389.55,
          "end": 393.6,
          "en": "Therefore, here we can use the useRef hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 393.6,
          "end": 396.54,
          "en": "which of course also must be imported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 396.54,
          "end": 399.663,
          "en": "to get our dialogue ref here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 400.98,
          "end": 404.15999999999997,
          "en": "And we connect that through the special ref prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 404.15999999999997,
          "end": 406.08299999999997,
          "en": "to that dialogue element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 407.55,
          "end": 410.07,
          "en": "And now in this open method here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 410.07,
          "end": 414.027,
          "en": "we can call dialogue.current.showModal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 416.85,
          "end": 418.92,
          "en": "And showModal is now a method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 418.92,
          "end": 421.623,
          "en": "provided by the built-in dialogue element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 423.72,
          "end": 425.82,
          "en": "But open is now a method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 425.82,
          "end": 429.423,
          "en": "provided by our component to other components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 430.32,
          "end": 433.23,
          "en": "Therefore, in this new project component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 433.23,
          "end": 435.72,
          "en": "we can now show the error modal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 435.72,
          "end": 438.123,
          "en": "by using this modal component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 438.96,
          "end": 443.403,
          "en": "And for that I'll add a fragment which wraps this div.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 444.87,
          "end": 449.61,
          "en": "And then also this newly added modal component here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 449.61,
          "end": 453.453,
          "en": "which of course must be imported from the Modal.jsx file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 456.15,
          "end": 460.413,
          "en": "And now we can connect this modal to a ref.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 461.85,
          "end": 464.85,
          "en": "Hence, I'll add another new ref here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 464.85,
          "end": 468.81,
          "en": "to my new project component, my modalRef,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 468.81,
          "end": 471.933,
          "en": "which will be connected to my own modal component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 473.28,
          "end": 476.46,
          "en": "And for that, we now simply add the ref prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 476.46,
          "end": 478.023,
          "en": "to our custom component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 478.95,
          "end": 483.66,
          "en": "which we can do since we're forwarding the refs in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 483.66,
          "end": 487.023,
          "en": "and I'll set this to modal, so to this ref I just added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 488.88,
          "end": 492.64,
